/col_dump.txt
/cols.txt

## scratch runtime caches (rebuildable)
scratch-pad-for-ai/rocm-cache-*/
scratch-pad-for-ai/uv-cache-*/

## vqapr-testbed: source is tracked, everything a run derives is not.
## workspace/ holds registered panels, materialized parquets and a workspace.yaml
## that grows with run length; outputs/ is measurement. Both are reproducible.
vqapr-testbed/workspace/
vqapr-testbed/outputs/

## vqapr-final-testbed: ONLY the staged environment is tracked -- the contract, the control
## files, the dependency pins. Nothing a run produces may ever be committed. A future run has
## to start from a clean slate, and a committed FINDINGS.md or build/ would hand the next agent
## the previous agent's answers, which is exactly what the isolation exists to prevent.
## (`build/` is already caught by the global rule above; it is named here so the exclusion reads
## as deliberate rather than incidental.)
vqapr-final-testbed/FINDINGS.md
vqapr-final-testbed/build/
